pylibfdt: use the Python 3 C-API names directly

scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i still calls PyString_FromString() and
PyInt_AsLong(). Those are Python 2 C-API names; they only ever compiled
under Python 3 because SWIG's pyhead.swg emitted compatibility macros
(PyString_FromString -> PyUnicode_FromString, PyInt_AsLong ->
PyLong_AsLong) into the generated wrapper.

SWIG 4.5.0 dropped that Python 2 compatibility block, so libfdt_wrap.c
now fails to build:

  libfdt_wrap.c:5618: error: implicit declaration of function 'PyInt_AsLong'
  libfdt_wrap.c:6679: error: implicit declaration of function 'PyString_FromString'
  libfdt_wrap.c:6679: error: assignment to 'PyObject *' from 'int' makes
                             pointer from integer without a cast

which breaks scripts_dtc, and with it every U-Boot build that has
CONFIG_PYLIBFDT=y (selected by CONFIG_BINMAN).

Call the Python 3 names the macros expanded to. Behaviour is unchanged;
U-Boot builds pylibfdt with $(PYTHON3) only, so the Python 2 spellings
had no remaining purpose.

Note the third Python 2 call, PyString_AsString() in the fdt_setprop()
typemap, needs no change: it sits in the %#else branch of a
PY_VERSION_HEX >= 0x03000000 test and is not compiled under Python 3.

Signed-off-by: Thingino <thingino@thingino.com>

--- a/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
+++ b/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
@@ -1033,7 +1033,7 @@
 	PyObject *buff;
 
 	if ($1) {
-		resultobj = PyString_FromString(
+		resultobj = PyUnicode_FromString(
 			fdt_string(fdt1, fdt32_to_cpu($1->nameoff)));
 		buff = PyByteArray_FromStringAndSize(
 			(const char *)($1 + 1), fdt32_to_cpu($1->len));
@@ -1070,7 +1070,7 @@
 
 /* typemaps used for fdt_next_node() */
 %typemap(in, numinputs=1) int *depth (int depth) {
-   depth = (int) PyInt_AsLong($input);
+   depth = (int) PyLong_AsLong($input);
    $1 = &depth;
 }
 
